#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"
msgstr "Installer Qiskit {#install-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Whether you will work locally or in a cloud environment, the first step for "
"all users is to install Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Que tu travailles en local ou dans un environnement cloud, la première étape"
" pour tous les utilisateurs est d'installer Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Upgrade from Qiskit 0.x to Qiskit 1.0 and beyond\">\n"
"  (If you are installing Qiskit for the first time, skip ahead to the [Install and set up](#local) section. This notice is relevant only to users who have installed Qiskit previously.)\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Mise à niveau de Qiskit 0.x vers Qiskit 1.0 et au-delà\">\n"
"  (Si tu installes Qiskit pour la première fois, passe directement à la section [Installer et configurer](#local). Cette remarque ne concerne que les utilisateurs ayant déjà installé Qiskit.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  **For those upgrading from version 0.x to 1.0 or later**: note that "
"because Qiskit v1.0 uses a new packaging structure, you **cannot** use `pip "
"install -U qiskit` to upgrade from any Qiskit 0.x version to 1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"  **Pour ceux qui mettent à niveau de la version 0.x vers 1.0 ou "
"ultérieure** : note que Qiskit v1.0 utilise une nouvelle structure de "
"paquets, donc tu **ne peux pas** utiliser `pip install -U qiskit` pour "
"passer de n'importe quelle version Qiskit 0.x à 1.0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  See the [Qiskit 1.0 migration guide](/guides/qiskit-1.0) for details and "
"instructions.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Consulte le [guide de migration Qiskit 1.0](/guides/qiskit-1.0) pour les "
"détails et les instructions.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Future updates starting with Qiskit 1.0 will allow for in-place upgrades.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Les futures mises à jour à partir de Qiskit 1.0 permettront des mises à niveau en place.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"local\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"local\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Qiskit SDK {#install-the-qiskit-sdk}"
msgstr "Installer le SDK Qiskit {#install-the-qiskit-sdk}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install Python. Check the \"Programming Language\" section on the [Qiskit "
"PyPI project page](https://pypi.org/project/qiskit/) to determine which "
"Python versions are supported by the most recent release. For download "
"instructions, see the [Python Beginners "
"Guide](https://wiki.python.org/moin/BeginnersGuide/Download).\n"
msgstr ""
"Installe Python. Consulte la section « Programming Language » sur la [page "
"du projet Qiskit sur PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/qiskit/) pour savoir "
"quelles versions de Python sont prises en charge par la version la plus "
"récente. Pour les instructions de téléchargement, voir le [Guide de "
"démarrage Python](https://wiki.python.org/moin/BeginnersGuide/Download).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    It is recommended that you use [Python virtual "
"environments](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html) to separate "
"Qiskit from other applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"    Il est recommandé d'utiliser des [environnements virtuels "
"Python](https://docs.python.org/3.10/tutorial/venv.html) pour isoler Qiskit "
"des autres applications.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    These instructions use the standard Python distribution from [pypi.org](https://pypi.org/). However, you can use other Python distributions, such as [Anaconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/anaconda/) or [miniconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/), along with other dependency management workflows like [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/docs/).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"    Ces instructions utilisent la distribution Python standard de [pypi.org](https://pypi.org/). Tu peux toutefois utiliser d'autres distributions Python, comme [Anaconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/anaconda/) ou [miniconda](https://docs.anaconda.com/miniconda/), ainsi que d'autres gestionnaires de dépendances tels que [Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/docs/).\n"
"    </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"If you're new to virtual environments, click to expand for more information.\">\n"
"    A virtual Python environment is an isolated space to work with Python for a specific purpose — so you can install whatever packages you wish, and set up libraries, dependencies, and so on, without affecting the \"base\" Python environment on your machine.\n"
msgstr ""
"    <Accordion>\n"
"    <AccordionItem title=\"Si tu débutes avec les environnements virtuels, clique ici pour en savoir plus.\">\n"
"    Un environnement virtuel Python est un espace isolé pour travailler avec Python dans un but précis — tu peux y installer les paquets que tu souhaites, configurer des bibliothèques, des dépendances, etc., sans affecter l'environnement Python « de base » de ta machine.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    One important advantage of a virtual environment is that if your Python "
"environment becomes corrupted somewhere along the way, you can easily delete"
" the virtual environment and start over!\n"
msgstr ""
"    Un avantage important d'un environnement virtuel est que si ton "
"environnement Python se retrouve corrompu, tu peux simplement supprimer "
"l'environnement virtuel et repartir de zéro !\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Choose a preferred location in which to store information about your virtual environments. Typically they're stored in a directory named `.venv` within each project directory you're working in.\n"
"    </AccordionItem>\n"
"    </Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"    Choisis un emplacement où stocker les informations relatives à tes environnements virtuels. En général, ils sont stockés dans un répertoire nommé `.venv` à l'intérieur de chaque répertoire de projet.\n"
"    </AccordionItem>\n"
"    </Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    First, navigate to your project directory and create a minimal "
"environment with only Python installed in it.\n"
msgstr ""
"    D'abord, navigue vers le répertoire de ton projet et crée un "
"environnement minimal avec uniquement Python d'installé.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"        <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"          <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```shell\n"
"            python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```shell\n"
"            python3 -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
msgstr "          <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"            ```text\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"            ```text\n"
"            python -m venv .venv\n"
"            ```\n"
"          </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    Next, activate your new environment.\n"
msgstr "    Ensuite, active ton nouvel environnement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"         <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"           <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"
msgstr ""
"         <OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
"           <TabItem value=\"mac\" label=\"macOS\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```shell\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```shell\n"
"             source .venv/bin/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "           <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"
msgstr "           <TabItem value=\"linux\" label=\"Linux\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"           <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
"              If using PowerShell:\n"
msgstr ""
"           <TabItem value=\"win\" label=\"Windows\">\n"
"              Si tu utilises PowerShell :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n"
"             ```\n"
"             If using Git Bash:\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\n"
"             ```\n"
"             Si tu utilises Git Bash :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             source .venv/scripts/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"              If using command prompt:\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             source .venv/scripts/activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"              Si tu utilises l'invite de commandes :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"             ```text\n"
"             .venv\\Scripts\\activate\n"
"             ```\n"
"           </TabItem>\n"
"         </OperatingSystemTabs>\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Install pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/) if it's not "
"already installed in your environment. Pip is a Python package manager that "
"you use to install Qiskit and other Python packages. Use `pip list` to see "
"what is in your virtual environment. In most Python environments, pip is "
"already installed.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Installe pip](https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/installation/) s'il n'est pas "
"déjà installé dans ton environnement. Pip est un gestionnaire de paquets "
"Python que tu utilises pour installer Qiskit et d'autres paquets Python. "
"Utilise `pip list` pour voir ce qui se trouve dans ton environnement "
"virtuel. Dans la plupart des environnements Python, pip est déjà installé.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the Qiskit SDK.\n"
msgstr "Installe le SDK Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install qiskit\n"
"      ```\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install qiskit\n"
"      ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      <Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Add visualization support\">\n"
"      If you intend to use visualization functionality or Jupyter notebooks, also install the `qiskit.visualization` module. See the [Visualizations API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization) for more information.\n"
"      </Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"      <Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Ajouter le support de visualisation\">\n"
"      Si tu comptes utiliser les fonctionnalités de visualisation ou des notebooks Jupyter, installe également le module `qiskit.visualization`. Consulte la [référence de l'API Visualizations](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/visualization) pour plus d'informations.\n"
"      </Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"local-jupyter\"></span>\n"
"1. If you want to run a Jupyter notebook with the Qiskit packages you just installed, you need to install Jupyter in your environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"<span id=\"local-jupyter\"></span>\n"
"1. Si tu veux exécuter un notebook Jupyter avec les paquets Qiskit que tu viens d'installer, tu dois installer Jupyter dans ton environnement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install jupyter\n"
"      ```\n"
"    Then open your notebook as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      pip install jupyter\n"
"      ```\n"
"    Puis ouvre ton notebook comme suit :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      jupyter notebook <path/to/notebook.ipynb>\n"
"      ```\n"
msgstr ""
"      ```shell\n"
"      jupyter notebook <path/to/notebook.ipynb>\n"
"      ```\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you are planning to work locally and use simulators built into Qiskit, "
"then your installation is done. If you want to run jobs on IBM&reg; QPUs, "
"continue on to [set up your IBM Cloud&reg; account](cloud-setup).\n"
msgstr ""
"Si tu prévois de travailler en local et d'utiliser les simulateurs intégrés "
"à Qiskit, ton installation est terminée. Si tu veux exécuter des tâches sur "
"des QPU IBM&reg;, continue vers la [configuration de ton compte IBM "
"Cloud&reg;](cloud-setup).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Stay current with the latest versions\">\n"
"Periodically check the [Qiskit release notes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes) to see new releases. We recommend frequently updating your requirements for `qiskit` by running `pip install -U qiskit`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Rester à jour avec les dernières versions\">\n"
"Consulte régulièrement les [notes de version de Qiskit](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/release-notes) pour découvrir les nouvelles versions. Nous recommandons de mettre fréquemment à jour tes dépendances pour `qiskit` en exécutant `pip install -U qiskit`.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshooting {#troubleshooting}"
msgstr "Dépannage {#troubleshooting}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`No Module 'qiskit'` error with Jupyter Notebook\">\n"
"  If you used ``pip install qiskit`` and set up your virtual environment in\n"
"  Anaconda, then you may get the ``No Module 'qiskit'`` error when you run a tutorial\n"
"  in Jupyter Notebook. If you have not installed Qiskit or set up your\n"
"  virtual environment, you can follow the [installation](#qiskit-install) steps.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"`No Module 'qiskit'` error with Jupyter Notebook\">\n"
"  Si tu as utilisé ``pip install qiskit`` et configuré ton environnement virtuel dans\n"
"  Anaconda, tu pourrais obtenir l'erreur ``No Module 'qiskit'`` quand tu lances un tutoriel\n"
"  dans Jupyter Notebook. Si tu n'as pas encore installé Qiskit ou configuré ton\n"
"  environnement virtuel, tu peux suivre les étapes d'[installation](#qiskit-install).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The error is caused when trying to import the Qiskit package in an\n"
"  environment where Qiskit is not installed. If you launched Jupyter Notebook\n"
"  from the Anaconda-Navigator, it is possible that Jupyter Notebook is running\n"
"  in the base (root) environment, instead of in your virtual\n"
"  environment. Choose a virtual environment in the Anaconda-Navigator from the\n"
"  **Applications on** dropdown menu. In this menu, you can see\n"
"  all of the virtual environments within Anaconda, and you can\n"
"  select the environment where you have Qiskit installed to launch Jupyter\n"
"  Notebook.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Cette erreur survient quand on essaie d'importer le paquet Qiskit dans un\n"
"  environnement où Qiskit n'est pas installé. Si tu as lancé Jupyter Notebook\n"
"  depuis Anaconda-Navigator, il est possible que Jupyter Notebook s'exécute\n"
"  dans l'environnement de base (root) plutôt que dans ton environnement\n"
"  virtuel. Choisis un environnement virtuel dans Anaconda-Navigator via le menu déroulant\n"
"  **Applications on**. Dans ce menu, tu peux voir\n"
"  tous les environnements virtuels disponibles dans Anaconda, et tu peux\n"
"  sélectionner l'environnement où Qiskit est installé pour lancer Jupyter\n"
"  Notebook.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Compilation errors during installation\">\n"
"  Qiskit depends on a number of other open-source Python packages, which\n"
"  are automatically installed when doing ``pip install qiskit``. Depending on\n"
"  your system's platform and Python version, it is possible that a particular\n"
"  package does not provide pre-built binaries for your system. You can refer\n"
"  to [Operating system support](#operating-system-support) for a list of platforms supported by Qiskit, some\n"
"  of which may need an extra compiler. In cases where there are\n"
"  no precompiled binaries available, ``pip`` will attempt to compile the package\n"
"  from source, which in turn might require some extra dependencies that need to\n"
"  be installed manually.\n"
msgstr ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Erreurs de compilation pendant l'installation\">\n"
"  Qiskit dépend d'un certain nombre d'autres paquets Python open source, qui\n"
"  sont automatiquement installés lors du ``pip install qiskit``. Selon\n"
"  la plateforme de ton système et la version de Python, il est possible qu'un paquet\n"
"  particulier ne propose pas de binaires précompilés pour ton système. Tu peux consulter\n"
"  [Support des systèmes d'exploitation](#operating-system-support) pour une liste des plateformes prises en charge par Qiskit, dont\n"
"  certaines peuvent nécessiter un compilateur supplémentaire. Dans les cas où il n'y a pas\n"
"  de binaires précompilés disponibles, ``pip`` tentera de compiler le paquet\n"
"  depuis les sources, ce qui peut nécessiter des dépendances supplémentaires à installer manuellement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  If the output of ``pip install qiskit`` contains similar lines to:\n"
msgstr ""
"  Si la sortie de ``pip install qiskit`` contient des lignes similaires à "
":\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  please check the documentation of the package that failed to install (in the\n"
"  example code, ``SOME_PACKAGE``) for information on how to install the libraries\n"
"  needed for compiling from source.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"  consulte la documentation du paquet qui a échoué à s'installer (dans l'exemple,\n"
"  ``SOME_PACKAGE``) pour savoir comment installer les bibliothèques\n"
"  nécessaires à la compilation depuis les sources.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"os-support\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"os-support\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Operating system support {#operating-system-support}"
msgstr "Support des systèmes d'exploitation {#operating-system-support}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit strives to support as many operating systems as possible, but due to "
"limitations in available testing resources and operating system "
"availability, not all operating systems can be supported. Operating system "
"support for Qiskit is broken into three tiers with different levels of "
"support for each tier. For platforms outside these, such as FreeBSD or "
"WebAssembly (WASI), Qiskit may still be installable, but it is not tested "
"and you will have to build Qiskit (and likely Qiskit’s dependencies) from "
"source.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit s'efforce de prendre en charge le plus grand nombre de systèmes "
"d'exploitation possible, mais en raison des limitations des ressources de "
"test disponibles et de la disponibilité des systèmes d'exploitation, tous ne"
" peuvent pas être pris en charge. Le support des systèmes d'exploitation "
"pour Qiskit est divisé en trois niveaux avec différents degrés de support "
"pour chaque niveau. Pour les plateformes hors de ces niveaux, comme FreeBSD "
"ou WebAssembly (WASI), Qiskit reste peut-être installable, mais il n'est pas"
" testé et tu devras le compiler (et probablement ses dépendances) depuis les"
" sources.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Additionally, Qiskit only supports the CPython implementation of the Python "
"language. Running with other Python interpreters such as PyPy is not "
"supported.\n"
msgstr ""
"De plus, Qiskit ne prend en charge que l'implémentation CPython du langage "
"Python. L'exécution avec d'autres interpréteurs Python tels que PyPy n'est "
"pas prise en charge.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit v2.x {#qiskit-v2x}"
msgstr "Qiskit v2.x {#qiskit-v2x}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the Qiskit v2.x release series, the supported platforms are:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans la série de versions Qiskit v2.x, les plateformes prises en charge sont"
" :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 1\">\n"
"  Tier 1 operating systems are fully tested as part of the development processes to ensure any proposed change will function correctly. Pre-compiled binaries are built, tested, and published to PyPI as part of the release process. Typically, as long as there is a functioning Python environment installed, Qiskit can be installed on these operating systems without needing to install further dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Niveau 1\">\n"
"  Les systèmes d'exploitation de niveau 1 sont entièrement testés dans le cadre du processus de développement pour s'assurer que toute modification proposée fonctionnera correctement. Des binaires précompilés sont construits, testés et publiés sur PyPI dans le cadre du processus de publication. En règle générale, tant qu'un environnement Python fonctionnel est installé, Qiskit peut être installé sur ces systèmes sans avoir à installer de dépendances supplémentaires.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 1 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Systèmes d'exploitation de niveau 1 :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Linux x86_64 (distributions compatible with the [manylinux "
"2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification).\n"
msgstr ""
"Linux x86_64 (distributions compatibles avec la spécification de packaging "
"[manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/)).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "macOS ARM64 (11.0 or newer)\n"
msgstr "macOS ARM64 (11.0 ou version ultérieure)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Windows 64-bit (Windows 10 and later supported)\n"
msgstr "Windows 64 bits (Windows 10 et versions ultérieures prises en charge)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - Linux AArch64 (distributions compatible with the [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 2\">\n"
"  Tier 2 operating systems are not tested as part of the development process. However, pre-compiled binaries are built, tested, and published to PyPI as part of the release process, and these packages can be expected to be installed with only a functioning Python environment.\n"
"  There might be a delay in releasing packages for these systems, since test failures might not be detected until much later, and failures during publishing will not block the publication of the package for Tier 1 systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"  - Linux AArch64 (distributions compatibles avec la spécification de packaging [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/))\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Niveau 2\">\n"
"  Les systèmes d'exploitation de niveau 2 ne sont pas testés dans le cadre du processus de développement. Cependant, des binaires précompilés sont construits, testés et publiés sur PyPI dans le cadre du processus de publication, et ces paquets peuvent normalement être installés avec seulement un environnement Python fonctionnel.\n"
"  Il peut y avoir un délai dans la publication des paquets pour ces systèmes, car les échecs de test risquent de n'être détectés que bien plus tard, et les échecs lors de la publication ne bloqueront pas la publication pour les systèmes de niveau 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 2 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Systèmes d'exploitation de niveau 2 :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - macOS x86_64 (10.12 or later)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Tier 3\">\n"
"  Tier 3 operating systems are not tested as part of the development process. Pre-compiled binaries are built and published to PyPI as part of the release process but are not tested. They may not be installable with only a functioning Python environment and might require a C/C++ compiler or additional programs to build dependencies from source as part of the installation process. Support for these operating systems are best effort only.\n"
msgstr ""
"  - macOS x86_64 (10.12 ou version ultérieure)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Niveau 3\">\n"
"  Les systèmes d'exploitation de niveau 3 ne sont pas testés dans le cadre du processus de développement. Des binaires précompilés sont construits et publiés sur PyPI dans le cadre du processus de publication, mais ne sont pas testés. Ils peuvent ne pas être installables avec un simple environnement Python fonctionnel et peuvent nécessiter un compilateur C/C++ ou des programmes supplémentaires pour compiler les dépendances depuis les sources lors de l'installation. Le support de ces systèmes d'exploitation est fourni sur la base du meilleur effort.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "  Tier 3 operating systems:\n"
msgstr "  Systèmes d'exploitation de niveau 3 :\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Linux ppc64le (distributions compatible with the [manylinux "
"2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/)packaging specification)\n"
msgstr ""
"Linux ppc64le (distributions compatibles avec la spécification de packaging "
"[manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/))\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - Linux s390x (distributions compatible with the [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/) packaging specification)\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"  - Linux s390x (distributions compatibles avec la spécification de packaging [manylinux 2014](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0599/))\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Starting in Qiskit v2.0.0, only 64-bit platforms are supported and 32-bit platforms are not supported. You will not be able to build from source\n"
"on 32-bit platforms either, as internally the Qiskit Rust code assumes a 64-bit pointer width.\n"
msgstr ""
"À partir de Qiskit v2.0.0, seules les plateformes 64 bits sont prises en "
"charge ; les plateformes 32 bits ne le sont plus. Tu ne pourras pas non plus"
" compiler depuis les sources sur des plateformes 32 bits, car le code Rust "
"interne de Qiskit suppose une largeur de pointeur 64 bits.\n"

